1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,766
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:06,766 --> 00:00:08,460
How do you do?

3
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:10,194
Hello.

4
00:00:10,194 --> 00:00:11,266
I'm Ralph Riley.

5
00:00:11,266 --> 00:00:13,882
I'm Richard Stewart, and this is my wife, Marilyn.

6
00:00:13,882 --> 00:00:14,523
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:14,523 --> 00:00:15,325
Likewise, Mr. Riley.

8
00:00:15,325 --> 00:00:20,076
Please, sit down. What can I do for you?

9
00:00:20,076 --> 00:00:22,863
We'd like to discuss a mortgage.

10
00:00:22,863 --> 00:00:23,795
For a house.

11
00:00:23,795 --> 00:00:26,170
Fine. Are you buying a house

12
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:28,075
or are you refinancing your present home?

13
00:00:28,075 --> 00:00:29,959
We're planning to buy a house.

14
00:00:29,959 --> 00:00:32,284
And we'd like to find out about a mortgage.

15
00:00:32,284 --> 00:00:34,229
We are customers of the bank.

16
00:00:34,229 --> 00:00:37,206
As a matter of fact, my whole family banks here.

17
00:00:37,206 --> 00:00:40,574
I have some questions to ask.

18
00:00:40,574 --> 00:00:43,079
Do you own your house or do you rent?

19
00:00:43,079 --> 00:00:44,032
Neither.

20
00:00:44,032 --> 00:00:49,103
We live with my parents, Dr. and Mrs. Philip Stewart.

21
00:00:49,103 --> 00:00:51,108
And how old are you?

22
00:00:51,108 --> 00:00:52,090
I'm twenty-nine.

23
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:54,566
I'm thirty.

24
00:00:54,566 --> 00:00:57,382
And, Mr. Stewart, what is your occupation?

25
00:00:57,382 --> 00:00:59,247
I'm a freelance photographer.

26
00:00:59,247 --> 00:01:00,780
And, Mrs. Stewart, are you working?

27
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:04,258
Yes. I'm a designer, and I work in a boutique.

28
00:01:04,258 --> 00:01:06,844
Did you bring any savings or salary information?

29
00:01:06,844 --> 00:01:08,097
Last year's tax forms?

30
00:01:08,097 --> 00:01:16,196
Yes. Here they are.

31
00:01:16,196 --> 00:01:18,892
OK. What ... what kind of house did you have in mind?

32
00:01:18,892 --> 00:01:20,015
We're talking about buying

33
00:01:20,015 --> 00:01:22,300
a two-bedroom house in Mount Kisco.

34
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:28,424
Here are the financial details on the house.

35
00:01:28,424 --> 00:01:29,356
Thank you.

36
00:01:29,356 --> 00:01:30,870
Are you prepared to make a ten-percent down payment?

37
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:32,644
Yes, we are.

38
00:01:32,644 --> 00:01:34,468
Payments over thirty years?

39
00:01:34,468 --> 00:01:38,337
Yes.

40
00:01:38,337 --> 00:01:40,772
Do you think we can get a loan?

41
00:01:40,772 --> 00:01:45,323
Well, it depends. Do you own any other property?

42
00:01:45,323 --> 00:01:48,440
Any stocks or bonds?

43
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:50,545
No.

44
00:01:50,545 --> 00:01:55,216
I see. Then you don't have any collateral.

45
00:01:55,216 --> 00:01:57,541
Perhaps you could get a guarantor--

46
00:01:57,541 --> 00:02:00,187
someone to sign for the loan for you.

47
00:02:00,187 --> 00:02:02,252
Why is that necessary?

48
00:02:02,252 --> 00:02:03,605
Since you don't have enough income,

49
00:02:03,605 --> 00:02:05,720
and you don't already own any property,

50
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:07,053
the bank needs to be sure

51
00:02:07,053 --> 00:02:08,957
you can pay the mortgage every month.

52
00:02:08,957 --> 00:02:10,952
A guarantor is responsible for the loan

53
00:02:10,952 --> 00:02:13,257
if you can't make the payments.

54
00:02:13,257 --> 00:02:20,143
I see. Well, the idea of buying a house is exciting.

55
00:02:20,143 --> 00:02:23,942
Thank you, Mr. Riley. We'll read this over carefully.

56
00:02:23,942 --> 00:02:25,004
Thank you.

57
00:02:25,004 --> 00:02:26,077
Good-bye. Thanks.

58
00:02:26,077 --> 00:02:29,695
Good-bye. And hope to see you soon.

59
00:02:29,695 --> 00:02:30,367
I hope so, too.

60
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:31,630
Take care.

61
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:51,676
Good-bye.

62
00:02:51,676 --> 00:02:52,578
It all sounded so easy

63
00:02:52,578 --> 00:02:56,818
until they mentioned needing collateral or a guarantor.

64
00:02:56,818 --> 00:02:59,845
We have no collateral.

65
00:02:59,845 --> 00:03:01,208
And I don't think it's a good idea

66
00:03:01,208 --> 00:03:04,415
to ask Dad to sign as a guarantor.

67
00:03:04,415 --> 00:03:05,989
I don't feel right about it.

68
00:03:05,989 --> 00:03:21,364
I understand your feelings about it, Richard.

69
00:03:21,364 --> 00:03:29,283
We can get a loan from the bank

70
00:03:29,283 --> 00:03:30,636
[03:25.43]if we can put up some collateral.

71
00:03:30,636 --> 00:03:32,881
And we don't own anything to use as collateral.

72
00:03:32,881 --> 00:03:38,514
Or someone can sign with us as a guarantor.

73
00:03:38,514 --> 00:03:40,428
Why don't you speak to Dad?

74
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:45,590
No. If we buy a house, I want to be able to handle it alone.

75
00:03:45,590 --> 00:03:48,788
Everybody needs help sometimes, Richard.

76
00:03:48,788 --> 00:03:50,963
I understand Richard's feelings about it, Ellen.

77
00:03:50,963 --> 00:03:53,809
In two or three months, I'll have an advance on my book

78
00:03:53,809 --> 00:03:56,856
and be able to put more money down.

79
00:03:56,856 --> 00:04:00,154
What about the house in Mount Kisco?

80
00:04:00,154 --> 00:04:02,219
Somebody else'll buy it by then.

81
00:04:02,219 --> 00:04:05,095
Then there'll be other houses, Marilyn.

82
00:04:05,095 --> 00:04:09,706
Richard has a point. You're just beginning to look. Richard

83
00:04:09,706 --> 00:04:10,768
We're in no great rush. It's true.

84
00:04:10,768 --> 00:04:12,953
This has been a great learning experience for us, Marilyn.

85
00:04:12,953 --> 00:04:15,048
Talking to the real-estate agent.

86
00:04:15,048 --> 00:04:17,404
Looking at the houses.

87
00:04:17,404 --> 00:04:21,233
Talking to the loan officer at the bank.

88
00:04:21,233 --> 00:04:23,367
It has been a learning experience. That's true.

89
00:04:23,367 --> 00:04:26,094
I think you're doing the right thing. Taking your time.

90
00:04:26,094 --> 00:04:29,542
Looking around. Especially with a purchase of this kind.

91
00:04:29,542 --> 00:04:33,110
You're talking about a lot of money.

92
00:04:33,110 --> 00:04:36,588
We'll call Mrs. Martinelli and tell her to keep looking for us.

93
00:04:36,588 --> 00:04:41,589
And I'll call Mr. Riley at the bank

94
00:04:41,589 --> 00:04:42,271
and tell him we'll see him in a couple of months.

95
00:04:42,271 --> 00:04:44,616
And if you ever need Dad or me to help you ...

96
00:04:44,616 --> 00:04:45,699
We know.

97
00:04:45,699 --> 00:04:47,884
You know we'll be there for you.

98
00:04:47,884 --> 00:04:47,884
It's a Stewart tradition. We're a family.
